<div class="bb-quote"><b>Jeysie wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">In the Gameplay Guide it says in the Player rules that a player can&#39;t take two turns in a row, then warns in the GM rules that the NPCs and threats can go twice (as a way to get the GM to encourage the heroes to mix up their initiatives a bit).
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
I don&#39;t have the set yet, but my understanding is that, while a specific enemy/group can&#39;t pick itself, you could have Hero 1 -&gt; Hero 2 -&gt; Hero 3 -&gt; Minion Group -&gt; Villain -&gt; Minion Group -&gt; Villain -&gt; Heroes

[/quote]

This is correct. (So generally you want to instead do something like Hero 1 &gt; Minions &gt; Hero 2 &gt; Villains &gt; Hero 3 &gt; (new turn) Hero 1 so the GM can&#39;t clump all their different threats in a row.&nbsp;
